3,3,44970,17,20,15,11,16,15,15,701,3944,1215,2383,20912,34,3,44970,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,701,925,1215,2383,20912,35,73315,4080,17,20,15,4999,16,15,15,701,16844,1215,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nRectangle $ABCD$ has center $O$ and $AB/AD=k$. A point is randomly chosen from the interior of rectangle $ABCD$. What is the probability that it is closer to $O$ than to any of the four vertices?  [asy]\nsize(200);\ndraw((-250,100)--(250,100)--(250,-100)--(-250,-100)--cycle);\ndot((0,0));\nlabel(\"$O$\",(0,0),N);\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-250,100),NW); label(\"$B$\",(250,100),NE); label(\"$C$\",(250,-100),SE); label(\"$D$\",(-250,-100),SW);[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9d471b9d0d4db906a7bb3d095e3b8ed9d1b764676f46c6a91f7206ad7107f69d"},"seconds":47.51881122589111,"seed":390269730128205459,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we begin by understanding the geometric conditions for a point within the rectangle to be closer to the center \\(O\\) than to any of the four vertices.\n\nLet the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) have dimensions \\(2a\\) by \\(2b\\) with \\(O\\) at \\((0,0)\\). The vertices of \\(ABCD\\) are:\n- \\(A = (-a, b)\\)\n- \\(B = (a, b)\\)\n- \\(C = (a, -b)\\)\n- \\(D = (-a, -b)\\)\n\nThe center \\(O\\) is located at \\((0,0)\\).\n\nFor a point \\((x, y)\\) to be closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex, the Euclidean distance from \\((x, y)\\) to \\(O\\) must be less than the distance to each of the vertices. Mathematically, for any vertex \\(V\\), this means:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} < \\sqrt{(x - x_V)^2 + (y - y_V)^2}\n\\]\nwhere \\((x_V, y_V)\\) are the coordinates of vertex \\(V\\).\n\nConsider the distance to vertex \\(A = (-a, b)\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} < \\sqrt{(x + a)^2 + (y - b)^2}\n\\]\n\nSquaring both sides, we get:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 < (x + a)^2 + (y - b)^2\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying:\n\\[\nx^2 + y^2 < x^2 + 2ax + a^2 + y^2 - 2by + b^2\n\\]\n\\[\n0 < 2ax + a^2 - 2by + b^2\n\\]\n\\[\n2ax - 2by < a^2 + b^2\n\\]\n\\[\nax - by < \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2}\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, we derive inequalities for the distances to the other vertices:\n\\[\nax + by < \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\n-ax + by < \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\n-ax - by < \\frac{a^2 + b^2}{2}\n\\]\n\nThese inequalities describe a smaller rectangle centered at \\(O\\) with side lengths \\(a'\\) and \\(b'\\) such that:\n\\[\na' = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\quad b' = \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\]\n\nThe area of the smaller rectangle is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of smaller rectangle} = a' \\times b' = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}} \\times \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{ab}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe area of the larger rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of larger rectangle} = 2a \\times 2b = 4ab\n\\]\n\nThe probability that a randomly chosen point in \\(ABCD\\) is closer to \\(O\\) than to any vertex is the ratio of the area of the smaller rectangle to the area of the larger rectangle:\n\\[\n\\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\frac{ab}{2}}{4ab} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
